  "$id": "https://ivrm.jp/contracts/herta-community-game-stats-read/v2",
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "description": "Producer Herta Studio; consumer server-only ivrm-web. POST /api/ivrm/community-game-stats/read. Key=HMAC-SHA256(IVRM_INTEGRATION_TOKEN,herta-community-game-stats-read-v1); signature=HMAC-SHA256(key,timestamp.eventId.POST.path.rawBody). Headers X-IVRM-Timestamp ISO, X-IVRM-Event-Id UUID, X-IVRM-Signature hex. Five-minute freshness, no query, max8192bytes. Signing is unchanged from v1 (the v1 purpose string remains the key-derivation domain separator); the contract version is negotiated by the signed request field version: absent or 1 returns exactly the v1 response (overviewResponse / userResponse), 2 returns the same game sections plus a required activity section (overviewResponseV2 / userResponseV2). The source of truth stays Herta community_game_activity_daily for games and community_activity_daily for activity; ivrm-web relays each read and stores no copy (ivrm-web #1703 S1/S4b, Herta #998). Request range from/to is a JST local_date range. mode is optional and defaults to overview: overview returns meta.earliestDate (the guild-wide first observed date, not range-limited), the top 25 games by totalSeconds with playerCount, and the user ranking paginated by limit/offset (max 100, ordered by totalSeconds desc then discordUserId asc; each entry carries its topGameName). mode=user requires discordUserId (and overview forbids it) and returns that user's totalSeconds plus their top 25 games. The v2 activity section is built only from the community_activity_daily metrics voice_seconds, messages and online_seconds (reactions are excluded: accumulated too sparsely). messages counts only the messages the bot's Activity Rules counted (cooldown-filtered), never the guild's raw message total; voice_seconds is stay time in countable voice channels; online_seconds is presence time and is a reference total only. overview activity carries guild totals for the range (voiceSeconds, messageCount, onlineSeconds, plus voiceMemberCount / messageMemberCount distinct-user counts) and the voice and message rankings, paginated by the same limit/offset as the game ranking (ordered by value desc then discordUserId asc). user activity carries only that user's voiceSeconds, messageCount and onlineSeconds for the range. Activity is fail-soft per section: when the activity read fails, activity is null while the game sections still return ok. All members are returned; opt-out filtering is applied by the ivrm-web relay, not here. Items carry aggregated seconds/counts only: no Rich Presence details/state, no message content, no raw session rows. All responses private,no-store.",
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/overviewResponse"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/userResponse"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/overviewResponseV2"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/userResponseV2"
    }
  ]
}
